// Address layout for x86_64 user programs and servers.
//
// Phase D.2: both programs (musl-linked, also native sysl) and
// servers load into the high user carve-out at VA 0x60000000 (same
// `prog.ld` / `server.ld` shape as aarch64). Per-process VMA
// layout (code + stack VMAs) is the single source of truth — see
// `oskit/kernel/vma.lsysl::VMA_DEFAULT_*`. Initial-SP / stack-low
// values are surfaced to PM and RS via
// `svc_vma_default_initial_sp` / `svc_vma_default_stack_low`
// (syscalls 96/97). The legacy `[0xCC000, 0x100000)` carve-out
// that used to back `SRV_USP/SRV_SSP = 0xD4000/0xD3000` is gone —
// servers now use the same `VMA_DEFAULT_STACK_TOP/_BOT` constants
// as everything else.
//
// PLATFORM_NAME (below) is the auxv `AT_PLATFORM` value — kept here
// because the prog build can't drag in cpu.lsysl's kernel externs.

module oskit.arch

// Legacy x86 server-stack constants. Equal to the cross-arch
// `VMA_DEFAULT_STACK_TOP/BOT` so RS's startup path can compute
// `child_sp = SRV_USP - 48` without importing the kernel VMA
// module. Deleted at the same time RS migrates to
// `svc_vma_default_initial_sp` directly.
val SRV_USP  = 0x60090000
val SRV_SSP  = 0x60080000

// AT_PLATFORM string for the SysV initial stack auxv. ld-musl reads
// this via `__init_libc` -> `__libc.platform` and uses it to pick
// HWCAP-gated string routines. Must match what musl was built for —
// we cross-build x86_64-slix-linux-musl, so the platform name is
// the unprefixed arch name.
val PLATFORM_NAME = "x86_64"
